   "id": "fefab7a93ab5e850ddcb90ac4c9d8eb351811fa0",
   "message": "fix(study): keep native wall stamps strictly increasing across host clock steps\n\nAttempt J's second pilot failed when the WSL realtime clock stepped back ~2 ms\nbetween a native decision and its path entry. A per-process strictly\nincreasing wall clock (fail-closed beyond 10 ms) now backs the probe and\nsource stamps; analytics and policy clients report peer close separately\nfrom truncation and accept a maximal 64 KiB reply.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
